# AGENTS.md

This file is the map for Cursor, Codex, and other AGENTS.md-aware tools. Claude Code: `CLAUDE.md` imports this file.

## Commands

- `just check` — format, lint, tests. This **is** the PR gate. Do not invent a second runner.
- `just test` — pytest only
- `just fmt` — apply ruff
{% if kind == 'service' %}
- `just up` — `docker compose up --build` (API{% if frontend == 'vite' %}, web{% endif %}{% if database == 'postgres' %}, Postgres{% endif %})
{% if frontend == 'vite' %}
- `just web` — Vite dev server (proxies `/api` to FastAPI on port 8000)
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% if evals != 'off' %}
- `just eval` — evaluation tests under `tests/evals/`
{% endif %}

If `just` is missing: `uv run ruff format --check src tests && uv run ruff check src tests && uv run pytest`

## Layout

{% if kind == 'service' %}
- `src/{{ package_name }}/api.py` — composition root: CORS, include routers. No route handlers.
- `src/{{ package_name }}/domain/` — product rules. No FastAPI, no database drivers.
- `src/{{ package_name }}/adapters/http/` — HTTP only. Calls domain. No SQL.
{% if database == 'postgres' %}
- `src/{{ package_name }}/adapters/postgres/` — the only package that uses `DATABASE_URL`
{% endif %}
{% if frontend == 'vite' %}
- `frontend/` — browser app. HTTP only, via `frontend/src/api.ts`
{% endif %}
{% else %}
- `src/{{ package_name }}/` — all runtime code
{% endif %}
- `tests/` — unit, architecture, and registry tests
- `docs/architecture/` — **only** place for living mermaid (context, runtime, data, flows)
- `docs/decisions/` — ADRs; do not edit old mermaid to match new code
- `docs/runbooks/` — how to run and recover, not architecture

## Do not

- Create `ARCHITECTURE.md` at the repo root
- Put mermaid in `README.md` or this file
- Push to `main` or `{{ integration_branch }}`
- Open an MR/PR against `main` unless you are merging `dev` → `main`{% if integration_branch == 'main' %} (this repo integrates on main; still use a feature branch){% endif %}
- Skip hooks, force-push shared branches, or commit `.env` / secrets
- Add a second tools/agents folder; extend the registry
{% if kind == 'service' %}
- Import `adapters` from `domain` (dependencies point inward)
- Put SQL or `DATABASE_URL` in HTTP adapters or the frontend
- Add a new deployable microservice unless the human asked — grow a capability here first
{% endif %}
{% if frontend == 'vite' %}- Import Python from `frontend/`, or query Postgres (or any database) from the browser
- Put `DATABASE_URL` or other connection strings in frontend code
- Serve product HTML from FastAPI; keep `/docs` as the API explorer only
{% endif %}{% if database == 'postgres' %}- Give the frontend a database driver or a connection string; the API is the only client of Postgres
{% endif %}

## Git

Branch from `origin/{{ integration_branch }}`. Name branches `feat/`, `fix/`, or `chore/`. Open a {{ 'merge request' if git_host == 'gitlab' else 'pull request' }} with base **{{ integration_branch }}**. Do not merge it unless the human asked.

{% if git_host == 'gitlab' %}
```bash
git checkout -b feat/short-name origin/{{ integration_branch }}
git push -u origin HEAD
glab mr create --target-branch {{ integration_branch }} --fill
```
{% else %}
```bash
git checkout -b feat/short-name origin/{{ integration_branch }}
git push -u origin HEAD
gh pr create --base {{ integration_branch }} --fill
```
{% endif %}

## When you change code

- Models or events → update `docs/architecture/data.md` in the same PR
- New process, worker, or service → `docs/architecture/runtime.md`
- New actor or external API → `docs/architecture/context.md`
{% if kind == 'service' %}
- New product capability → `domain/<name>.py` + `adapters/http/<name>.py`, then `include_router` in `adapters/http/router.py`
{% endif %}
{% if kind != 'package' %}- New tool → register it in `src/{{ package_name }}/registry.py` and add `tests/test_tool_<name>.py`
{% endif %}{% if frontend == 'vite' %}- New HTTP route → add it on FastAPI **and** a function in `frontend/src/api.ts` in the same PR
{% endif %}{% if database == 'postgres' %}- Schema or stored shape → `adapters/postgres/` only; update `docs/architecture/data.md`
{% endif %}- `just check` must pass before you stop

## Definition of done

`just check` is green. Architecture tests pass. Docs for the change are updated. The MR/PR targets `{{ integration_branch }}`.
